{
  "id": "hadith-corpus-labels-v0",
  "status": "v0-draft",
  "$comment": "The curated corpus-label index: every hadith address the Golden Set and the matn-identity map name, with the comparison-form label the citation gate builds, its collection, number and consolidated grade (the repo's fold over the Arabic edition's per-grader grades). It is a second hand-written declaration, not an independent source — no test process reads the corpus — so what it catches is drift among the three curated files: an address added to a row, a set or a map without being registered here, or a grade pinned differently. It cannot catch a label the curator misread in the corpus and wrote into both files; that residual risk is stated, not hidden. Each entry names the edition files it was read in — the Arabic edition whose row and grades the label comes from, and the Indonesian edition of the same collection it was matched to — with both files' SHA256 as recorded in the corpus manifest at curation time, so a changed corpus or a re-read can be audited against the recorded file. Source: hadith/ara-*.json and hadith/ind-*.json under the corpus root (fawazahmed0/hadith-api, Unlicense). Not gate data: it widens nothing.",
